  Don't re-read spells until you need to.  A sacrifest is a good 
time to let a lot of non-critical spells expire, so they'll be 
synchronized when you start descending again.  Timing the end
of the sacrifest with the end of a critical spell or two is not
a bad idea.  NB: The only spell critical to a sacrifest is create
monster, so....

  Remember, a given spellbook can only be read three times.  
(There's an exception:  A spell you don't know can, I believe,
be read from an otherwise exhausted spell book.  This may be to
make (master) mind flayers less of a disaster for spellcasters.)

  Name each spellbook twice when you read it.  Once individually
with number of times read and turn read: 2:65308.  Then 
non-individually with just the turn count:  65308.  The '\' 
command will then show the last time read of each spell.
Copy/paste the output into a decent editor, with macros.
Re-arrange the spellbook data so that the turn read is in front,
then sort.  You'll have all the spellbooks in the order by which
they'll expire, 20k turns after they were read.

  NB: Leave one spell expired for the endgame.  

