  Here's another possible use for wizard lock while foocubus 
dancing:

   |...
###-
##0....
 ##-
   |...

   The '|' are walls, '.' are floor, '0' is a boulder.  '#' are 
corridor.  '-' shows the edges of an open doorway.

   If you stand just to the right of the boulder you can interact
with a foocubi above or below the boulder, but the foocubi cannot
come in (without teleporting).   (I call it an "interaction 
nook".  The phrase coming from _The Gripping Hand_.)

   With skilled spell of detect monster going you can wander
over to the nook whenever a possible partner is nearby.  
Especially useful if you have multiple possible partners around.

   Might use spell of charm monster on foocubi of the wrong 
gender to make them peaceful, then teleport them away.
Later use amulet of change to make them useful.  Anger them
so they'll start coming to you.  I've never actually done this,
but it should work.  In my current game I've been leading 
soldiers from Ft. Ludious to my altar: self-portable sacrifices
bearing equipment.

   As a chaotic, same-race sacrifice summons peaceful major 
demons.  (You're neutral.  Don't do it.)  The first two will
be Yeenoghu and Juiblex.  Since they're peaceful you can just
lead them up/down stairs.  

  After that there's a good chance of foocubi summoning.  In my 
game I've got about twenty foocubi wandering around the level, 
most of them the wrong gender (and peaceful).  NB: The age of
the same race corpse doesn't matter: zombie and mummy corpses
always work.

  As I said before, max Con & Wis to get the most out of level
gains.  Don't stop at experience level 30.  A +1 ring of 
adornment will give your character complete control over any 
interaction. (+2 if you get a HoB).  All you need to take off for
an interaction is cloak and body armor.

  Name your foocubi (using 'C'all) so you can keep track of them.
(It can also add a certain...interest.)

